{
  "id": "inlay_hints/type_hints/08_explicit_initializers",
  "topic": "inlay_hints",
  "subtopic": "type_hints",
  "title": "Explicitly spelled initializers",
  "summary": "A type the initializer already names gets no hint",
  "prose": "A cast, a functional cast, a `new`, a factory naming the type as its template argument (`make_owner<Box<int>>()` for an `Owner<Box<int>>`) and a lambda all say what the variable holds. A class template whose arguments the initializer leaves to deduction shows them where it is written instead, and a factory whose result has arguments the call does not name still hints. `inlay_hints.spelled_types` shows every hint.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [
    "clangd#1749",
    "clangd#2603"
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "template <typename T>\nstruct Box {\n    Box(T first, T second);\n};\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nstruct Owner {};\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nOwner<T> make_owner();\n\ntemplate <typename T, typename U>\nstruct Table {};\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nTable<T, int> make_table();\n\nint compute();\n\nvoid use() {\n    auto widened = static_cast<long>(compute());\n    auto braced = int{42};\n    auto boxed = Box<int>(1, 2);\n    auto listed = Box<int>{3, 4};\n    auto grouped = (long{5});\n    auto created = new Box<int>(5, 6);\n    auto owned = make_owner<Box<int>>();\n    auto closure = [] { return 7; };\n    auto plain = compute();\n    auto inferred = Box(1, 2);\n    auto copied = auto(plain);\n    auto table = make_table<long>();\n}\n",
      "markers": [
        {
          "name": "spelled",
          "begin": 289,
          "end": 574,
          "range": true
        },
